Does it make sense to have {mifsle} be a block of code and {mivmifsle} be a
codon? Since I don't expect "code that is alive" to be a likely context, it
makes sense to me as "code for living things".
(Relatedly, does {mivmifra} make sense for DNA, RNA, or similar?)

Additionally, wouldn't the default place structure of {mifsle} start with
s1, the indivisible subunit?

 -Joe Anderson


